## Extras > Catalogue (chrome/catalogue.yaml, PxCatalogueWidget).
## Stats, weapons, features and who can build what are read from the rules; only these texts are hand-written.
## Keys: catalogue-<actor id, lower case, dots as dashes> with .role (short class line) and .lore (field dossier).
## A unit without an entry still shows, with a default role and its sidebar description.

button-px-catalogue = Catalogue

## Nations
catalogue-nation-usa =
    .lore = The Union's arsenal of democracy: the widest air wing in the world, supercarriers, the HIMAX rocket truck and the AB-35 Longwing that drops the Fatman atomic bomb.
catalogue-nation-england =
    .lore = Masters of deception: MI6 spies, gadget-packed Spy Cars and gap generators that blind the enemy.
catalogue-nation-france =
    .lore = Precision and stealth: GPS-guided LRX rockets, Rafale fighters and the cloaking Phase Transport.
catalogue-nation-germany =
    .lore = Engineers of time: Chrono Tanks that blink across the map and MARZ launchers that seed minefields.
catalogue-nation-japan =
    .lore = An island navy: the Kaga jump-jet carrier and Sea Arrow trucks that sink ships far out at sea.
catalogue-nation-southkorea =
    .lore = Peninsula shield: Chunmu launchers that switch between rocket salvos and one heavy guided missile.
catalogue-nation-italy =
    .lore = Mediterranean legion: the Cavour light carrier and the fast-reloading Saetta rocket launcher.
catalogue-nation-egypt =
    .lore = Desert command: cheap Mistral helicopter carriers and Saqr-36 cluster rockets that shred light vehicles.
catalogue-nation-russia =
    .lore = Tesla weapons: Shock Troopers, Tesla Tanks, the Kuznetsov carrier and the thermobaric TOZ-1 Sunflare.
catalogue-nation-ukraine =
    .lore = Demolitions: nuclear Demolition Trucks, Parabomb runs, the giant An-225 and precise Vilkra rockets.
catalogue-nation-cuba =
    .lore = Island fortress: rugged old Grad launchers fired in numbers and a defence built to outlast any siege.
catalogue-nation-india =
    .lore = Rising power: the home-built Vikrant carrier and Pinak launchers that empty their pods in seconds.
catalogue-nation-china =
    .lore = Red dragon: the Fujian supercarrier, the JX-20 stealth fighter and the PHX-16, longest-range launcher of all.
catalogue-nation-turkey =
    .lore = Gateway of continents: drone warfare from the Anadolu carrier, Swarm Drones and heavy Kasirga rockets.
catalogue-nation-pakistan =
    .lore = Mountain defenders: Fatah guided rockets that hit hard and true from deep behind the front.
catalogue-nation-iran =
    .lore = Drone masters: the Bagheri drone carrier, Shard attack drones and the Qahir-X stealth prototype.

## Structures
catalogue-fact =
    .role = Base command
    .lore = The heart of every base. It builds all other structures and sets your build radius, so losing it stops all expansion. Keep it deep inside your defences and, if the lobby allows it, pack it back into an MCV to move your base.
catalogue-powr =
    .role = Power generation
    .lore = Basic power for your base. Defences, radar and superweapons shut down on low power, so build plants ahead of demand and spread them out: a single strike on a cluster of plants can black out the whole base.
catalogue-apwr =
    .role = Heavy power generation
    .lore = Twice the output of a Power Plant on a larger footprint. A prime target for enemy bombers, so guard it with anti-air.
catalogue-proc =
    .role = Economy
    .lore = Turns ore and gems into credits and comes with a free Ore Truck. Build it close to rich fields to shorten each trip. A second refinery near another field almost doubles your income.
catalogue-silo =
    .role = Economy storage
    .lore = Extra storage for refined credits. Without enough storage, ore delivered beyond your limit is wasted. Cheap, so build one whenever your income outgrows storage.
catalogue-oilr =
    .role = Offshore economy
    .lore = A water platform that pumps a steady trickle of credits with no trucks to protect. It must be built on water next to your base and stops pumping on low power. Ships and submarines are its biggest threat.
catalogue-tent =
    .role = Infantry production
    .lore = Union barracks: trains riflemen, rocket soldiers, engineers, medics and the robot infantry. Several barracks speed up training. Set a rally point so fresh squads march straight to the front.
catalogue-barr =
    .role = Infantry production
    .lore = Vanguard barracks: trains conscripts, grenadiers, flame troops, Shock Troopers and the Iron Guard exosuits. Several barracks speed up training.
catalogue-kenn =
    .role = Dog training
    .lore = Trains attack dogs: fast, cheap hunters that kill infantry in one bite and sniff out disguised spies.
catalogue-weap =
    .role = Vehicle production
    .lore = Builds every tank, transport and rocket launcher. Add a Service Depot and a Radar Dome to unlock the heavier designs, including your nation's own rocket launcher.
catalogue-fix =
    .role = Field repair
    .lore = Repairs vehicles that drive onto its pad, for a fee. It also unlocks advanced vehicles. Place it between the War Factory and the front so damaged tanks get back into the fight quickly.
catalogue-dome =
    .role = Intelligence
    .lore = Turns on your radar minimap and unlocks most mid-tier units and defences. It also gives your long-range SAMs their full reach. Losing it blinds you, so guard it.
catalogue-hpad =
    .role = Helicopter base
    .lore = Builds and rearms helicopters. Each pad services one helicopter at a time, so build one per gunship you plan to field.
catalogue-afld =
    .role = Air base
    .lore = Builds and rearms jets, with parking for 4 planes. It also gives the Spy Plane and Paratrooper support powers. Fighters return here to reload after each sortie.
catalogue-abas =
    .role = Large air base
    .lore = A bigger airfield with parking for 6 planes. Expand your air wing without spreading pads across the base.
catalogue-afbs =
    .role = Air force base
    .lore = A full air force base with parking for 8 planes for a serious strike wing.
catalogue-sacm =
    .role = Strategic air command
    .lore = The crown of an air force: parking for 10 planes in one compound. Only one can be built, so defend it as well as your Construction Yard.
catalogue-atek =
    .role = Advanced research
    .lore = Union research centre. It unlocks the most advanced Union weapons and launches the GPS Satellite, which reveals the whole map.
catalogue-stek =
    .role = Advanced research
    .lore = Vanguard research centre. It unlocks the heaviest Vanguard tanks, Tesla weapons and the best jets.
catalogue-syrd =
    .role = Naval production
    .lore = Union shipyard. It builds and repairs gunboats, destroyers, cruisers, transports and, for some nations, aircraft carriers. It must be built on water.
catalogue-spen =
    .role = Naval production
    .lore = Vanguard submarine pen. It builds and repairs submarines, transports and Vanguard carriers. It must be built on water.
catalogue-gap =
    .role = Counter-intelligence
    .lore = Wraps your base in shroud so the enemy cannot see what is inside. Scouts and spy planes reveal it only briefly. It needs power.
catalogue-mslo =
    .role = Superweapon
    .lore = A nuclear missile silo. After a long charge it launches an atom bomb that flattens a whole district of an enemy base. Only one can be built, and every opponent is warned when it is ready.
catalogue-iron =
    .role = Superweapon
    .lore = Makes a group of units or buildings invulnerable for a short time. Time it with a tank push so the spearhead arrives untouchable.
catalogue-mi6 =
    .role = Intelligence headquarters
    .lore = British secret service headquarters. It unlocks the Spy and the Spy Cars. England only, one per player, and it needs power.
catalogue-supl =
    .role = Satellite control
    .lore = Ground control for your satellites. If you lose every Uplink, all your satellites go offline until you build a new one, so build a spare far from the front.
catalogue-lnch =
    .role = Space launch
    .lore = Builds and launches satellites from the Aircraft tab, up to 8 in orbit. The gateway to the orbital laser mesh.

## Defences
catalogue-sbag =
    .role = Light barrier
    .lore = Cheap sandbags that stop infantry and light vehicles and steer attackers into your guns. Tanks crush them.
catalogue-fenc =
    .role = Light barrier
    .lore = Barbed wire that stops infantry and light vehicles. Tanks crush it.
catalogue-brik =
    .role = Heavy barrier
    .lore = Concrete walls that stop every ground unit and block enemy fire. Only the Mammoth Tank can crush them. Use them to protect power plants and refineries.
catalogue-pbox =
    .role = Anti-infantry bunker
    .lore = A concrete pillbox with a machine gun. It sees stealth units and cuts down infantry rushes. Pair it with an anti-tank turret.
catalogue-hbox =
    .role = Camouflaged bunker
    .lore = A pillbox hidden under camouflage. Enemies don't see it until they are close, so it is a perfect ambush on a likely attack route.
catalogue-gun =
    .role = Anti-armour turret
    .lore = A rotating cannon turret that punches through tanks. Cheap and reliable, but weak against massed infantry and helpless against aircraft.
catalogue-ftur =
    .role = Anti-infantry tower
    .lore = Pours burning fuel over anyone who gets close. It ruins infantry and light vehicles, but has short range and can't touch tanks at a distance.
catalogue-tsla =
    .role = Tesla defence
    .lore = Hurls lightning that destroys infantry and vehicles alike. It needs a lot of power, and a blackout switches it off, so protect your plants.
catalogue-agun =
    .role = Short-range air defence
    .lore = A flak cannon that shreds aircraft, drones and incoming cruise missiles at short range. It needs power. Ring your base with them against bombers.
catalogue-sam =
    .role = Short-range air defence
    .lore = Launches surface-to-air missiles at aircraft and drones, and can shoot down some rockets and cruise missiles. It needs power.
catalogue-msam =
    .role = Medium-range air defence
    .lore = A medium-range missile battery that intercepts aircraft, cruise missiles, drones and some rockets. Reaches full range only with a Radar Dome. Place it so its coverage overlaps your SAMs.
catalogue-lsam =
    .role = Long-range air defence
    .lore = Patriot / S-400 class. It stops aircraft, cruise missiles and tactical ballistic missiles far beyond your base edge. Needs a Radar Dome for full range.
catalogue-bmd =
    .role = Ballistic missile defence
    .lore = THAAD class. It intercepts ballistic and hypersonic missiles high and far out, the only real answer to enemy rocket artillery and missile strikes. Needs a Radar Dome for full range.
catalogue-ptwr =
    .role = Prism defence
    .lore = Fires a crystal light beam. Nearby Prism Towers link up and feed their energy into the one that fires: +40% damage per linked tower, up to +200%. Build them in clusters.
catalogue-asat =
    .role = Anti-satellite
    .lore = Shoots down enemy satellites overhead within 12 cells. It can't hit ground units or aircraft. Your only defence against an orbital laser mesh.

## Infantry
catalogue-e1 =
    .role = Rifle infantry
    .lore = The backbone of every army: cheap, quick to train and good against other infantry. Garrison them in pillboxes, or mass them to screen your tanks from rocket soldiers.
catalogue-e2 =
    .role = Grenadier
    .lore = Lobs grenades that splash groups of infantry and damage buildings. Their grenades can hurt friendly units nearby, so keep them behind the front line.
catalogue-e3 =
    .role = Anti-tank / anti-air
    .lore = Shoulder-fired rockets that hit both armour and aircraft. Cheap, and the infantry answer to tanks and helicopters, but easy prey for machine guns.
catalogue-e4 =
    .role = Flame trooper
    .lore = Short-range flamethrowers that burn infantry in cover and set buildings ablaze. Strong for clearing bunkers and assaulting bases.
catalogue-e6 =
    .role = Engineer
    .lore = Captures enemy buildings, repairs your own and fixes broken bridges. Escort them into the enemy base and take a War Factory or Tech Center to steal its technology.
catalogue-spy =
    .role = Infiltrator
    .lore = Disguises as an enemy soldier and infiltrates buildings: steal cash from a refinery, reset superweapons, blind a radar or learn production secrets. Dogs see through the disguise.
catalogue-e7 =
    .role = Elite commando
    .lore = Tanya: dual pistols that drop infantry in one shot, and C4 that levels any building she reaches. Only one can be fielded. Keep her away from tanks and dogs.
catalogue-medi =
    .role = Field medic
    .lore = Heals nearby infantry in the field. Keep one with every infantry group and your squads survive much longer.
catalogue-mech =
    .role = Field mechanic
    .lore = Repairs vehicles in the field, keeping your tanks fighting far from a Service Depot.
catalogue-snip =
    .role = Marksman
    .lore = A long-range marksman who kills most infantry with one shot and hides when standing still. Deadly in overwatch, useless against armour.
catalogue-shok =
    .role = Tesla trooper
    .lore = Elite infantry with portable Tesla coils that arc through infantry and vehicles alike. Russia's signature soldier.
catalogue-dog =
    .role = Attack dog
    .lore = Fast and cheap, it kills infantry in one bite and sniffs out disguised spies. Keep a pair at home as spy hunters.
catalogue-cybt =
    .role = Cyborg infantry
    .lore = An armoured Union cyborg with a heavy auto-pistol. It can't be crushed by tanks and never needs cover. A tough line holder.
catalogue-bdrd =
    .role = Combat droid
    .lore = Cheap Union droids with forearm blasters, built in numbers. Use them to swamp enemy infantry and absorb fire.
catalogue-rgun =
    .role = Anti-armour robot
    .lore = Its railgun hits armour from long range but recharges slowly. Keep it behind a screen of infantry and let it pick off tanks.
catalogue-irgd =
    .role = Exosuit infantry
    .lore = A Vanguard soldier in a powered exosuit with a belt-fed heavy machine gun. Tanks can't crush it, and it mows down infantry.
catalogue-taut =
    .role = Tesla robot
    .lore = A clanking Vanguard robot that throws Tesla lightning from its claws, deadly to infantry and enemy robots.

## Vehicles
catalogue-1tnk =
    .role = Light tank
    .lore = Fast and cheap, ideal for scouting, harassing ore trucks and catching light vehicles. It loses a straight fight with heavier tanks.
catalogue-2tnk =
    .role = Main battle tank
    .lore = The Union's main battle tank: a good balance of speed, armour and firepower. Mass them with rocket soldiers and Mobile Flak for a complete army.
catalogue-3tnk =
    .role = Heavy tank
    .lore = The Vanguard's main battle tank with twin heavy cannons. Slower than Union armour but hits much harder. Wins head-on tank battles.
catalogue-4tnk =
    .role = Super-heavy tank
    .lore = The Mammoth: twin cannons for tanks, missile pods for aircraft and infantry, heavy armour and self-repair when damaged. Slow and expensive, and it crushes even concrete walls.
catalogue-mtnk =
    .role = Medium tank
    .lore = A cheaper Vanguard battle tank that is quicker to build than the Heavy Tank, with a lighter gun.
catalogue-arty =
    .role = Artillery
    .lore = Long-range howitzer that shells defences and infantry from beyond their reach. Very fragile up close, so always keep an escort.
catalogue-v2rl =
    .role = Rocket artillery
    .lore = Fires one huge rocket that devastates infantry and buildings from long range. Slow to reload and weak to anything that reaches it.
catalogue-harv =
    .role = Ore truck
    .lore = Collects ore and gems and brings them to your refinery. Heavily armoured, but unarmed. Protect your trucks: they are your income.
catalogue-mcv =
    .role = Mobile construction
    .lore = Deploys into a Construction Yard. Use it to open a second base near a distant ore field, or to rebuild after a disaster.
catalogue-jeep =
    .role = Scout vehicle
    .lore = The Ranger: a fast scout with a machine gun that carries one soldier. Use it to scout, chase infantry and hunt ore trucks.
catalogue-apc =
    .role = Armoured transport
    .lore = Carries a squad of infantry under armour and supports it with a machine gun. Drop engineers into an enemy base or rush rocket soldiers to the front.
catalogue-mnly =
    .role = Minelayer
    .lore = Lays anti-tank and anti-personnel mines and can see enemy mines. Seed ore fields and choke points to make every attack expensive.
catalogue-truk =
    .role = Supply truck
    .lore = Carries cash to an allied player's refinery. Unarmed. Use it to keep a struggling teammate in the game.
catalogue-mgg =
    .role = Mobile gap generator
    .lore = Covers the area around it in shroud. Drive it along with your army so the enemy can't see the attack coming.
catalogue-mrj =
    .role = Radar jammer
    .lore = Jams nearby enemy Radar Domes and deflects incoming guided missiles. Escort your armour into missile-heavy defences with it.
catalogue-ttnk =
    .role = Tesla tank
    .lore = A tank with a mounted Tesla coil whose lightning arcs through infantry, vehicles and buildings. Russia's answer to massed armour.
catalogue-ftrk =
    .role = Mobile anti-air
    .lore = A truck-mounted flak cannon that shreds aircraft, drones and infantry. Keep one with every armoured column.
catalogue-dtrk =
    .role = Nuclear bomb truck
    .lore = A truck with an armed nuclear warhead and paper-thin armour. Drive it into the enemy base and detonate it. It takes everything nearby with it, including your own units.
catalogue-ctnk =
    .role = Chrono tank
    .lore = Fires anti-ground missiles and can teleport anywhere within range. Blink behind enemy lines to strike artillery and refineries, then blink out.
catalogue-qtnk =
    .role = Seismic tank
    .lore = The MAD Tank shakes the ground with seismic waves that wreck nearby vehicles and structures, and destroys itself in the process. Drive it into the middle of an enemy base.
catalogue-stnk =
    .role = Stealth transport
    .lore = A light armoured transport that cloaks when idle and fires anti-ground missiles. Slip a squad of engineers past defences unseen.
catalogue-ptnk =
    .role = Prism tank
    .lore = A long-range beam tank whose crystal light beam splashes groups of infantry, light vehicles and buildings. Fragile, so keep it behind your heavy armour.
catalogue-enfw =
    .role = Assault walker
    .lore = A heavy two-legged Union walker. Twin arm autocannons shred infantry and a shoulder rocket pod cracks armour. A walking fortress for breaking defensive lines.
catalogue-strd =
    .role = Assault walker
    .lore = A slow four-legged Vanguard walker with a heavy cannon and a machine gun. It walks through infantry and outguns most tanks.
catalogue-sdrn =
    .role = Suicide drone
    .lore = A fast, cheap spider drone that runs at its target and detonates. Send waves of them at tank columns and robot armies.
catalogue-scar =
    .role = Spy vehicle
    .lore = A luxury car with hidden machine guns and pop-up rockets that carries one Spy. Enemies see a harmless civilian car until it attacks. Needs the MI6 Headquarters.
catalogue-scr2 =
    .role = Spy vehicle
    .lore = A classic grand tourer with hidden twin machine guns that carries one Spy. Tougher and cheaper than Spy Car 1. Needs the MI6 Headquarters.
catalogue-himax =
    .role = Rocket launcher (USA)
    .lore = A fast wheeled launcher with long-range guided rockets. It shoots and scoots, driving off after each launch, so counter-fire usually hits empty ground.
catalogue-hailstorm =
    .role = Rocket launcher (England)
    .lore = A tracked launcher that fires a big 12-rocket salvo over a wide area. Strong against infantry and bases, but slow.
catalogue-lrx =
    .role = Rocket launcher (France)
    .lore = A tracked launcher with GPS-guided rockets. Precise, with +50% damage against buildings. The best tool for picking apart defences.
catalogue-marz =
    .role = Rocket launcher (Germany)
    .lore = A tracked launcher with a 12-rocket salvo. Deploy it to switch to mine rockets that scatter anti-tank mines across the enemy's path.
catalogue-saetta =
    .role = Rocket launcher (Italy)
    .lore = A cheaper tracked launcher that reloads faster. Several Saettas firing in turn keep up constant pressure.
catalogue-kasirga =
    .role = Rocket launcher (Turkey)
    .lore = Heavy 300 mm rockets with very long range that crush buildings and grouped units. Slow to reload.
catalogue-fatah =
    .role = Rocket launcher (Pakistan)
    .lore = Guided long-range rockets that are very accurate against buildings, infantry and vehicles alike. Slow to reload.
catalogue-type12 =
    .role = Anti-ship missiles (Japan)
    .lore = A missile truck that hits ships far out at sea. Keep it on the coast and enemy fleets can't come close.
catalogue-chunmu =
    .role = Rocket launcher (South Korea)
    .lore = A heavy wheeled launcher with a 6-rocket salvo. Deploy it to switch to one heavy guided missile with longer range.
catalogue-toz1 =
    .role = Thermobaric launcher (Russia)
    .lore = An armoured thermobaric launcher. Short range, but it burns out infantry and buildings in a huge fireball.
catalogue-vilkra =
    .role = Rocket launcher (Ukraine)
    .lore = Precision long-range rockets that strike buildings, infantry and vehicles with surgical accuracy. Slow to reload.
catalogue-grad =
    .role = Rocket launcher (Cuba)
    .lore = An old Grad launcher: cheap but inaccurate. Mass them and saturate an area with rockets.
catalogue-pinak =
    .role = Rocket launcher (India)
    .lore = Fires its whole rocket load in seconds. A devastating surprise volley against infantry and bases.
catalogue-saqr36 =
    .role = Cluster launcher (Egypt)
    .lore = Cluster rockets that split into bomblets over the target. Ruinous for infantry and light vehicles, weak against tanks and buildings.
catalogue-phx16 =
    .role = Rocket launcher (China)
    .lore = The longest-range rocket launcher in the game. It shells bases and groups from far behind the front. Slow to reload.
catalogue-fajir5 =
    .role = Rocket launcher (Iran)
    .lore = Long range for a low price, but inaccurate. Deploy it to switch to two Shard-136 attack drones with very long range.

## Aircraft
catalogue-heli =
    .role = Attack helicopter
    .lore = The Longbow: a missile gunship that hunts tanks, buildings and other aircraft. Hit and run, then return to the Helipad to rearm.
catalogue-mh60 =
    .role = Assault helicopter
    .lore = The Black Hawk: a gunship with dual chain guns for infantry and light vehicles. Fast to rearm and great for clearing infantry.
catalogue-hind =
    .role = Assault helicopter
    .lore = The Hind: a heavy gunship with chain guns that mows down infantry and light vehicles.
catalogue-tran =
    .role = Transport helicopter
    .lore = The Chinook: carries a squad of infantry anywhere on the map. Unarmed, so drop your troops away from anti-air.
catalogue-mig =
    .role = Strike jet
    .lore = A fast ground-attack plane with missiles for buildings and vehicles. Strike, then fly back to the Airfield to rearm.
catalogue-yak =
    .role = Strafing jet
    .lore = An attack plane with dual machine guns that strafes infantry and light armour.
catalogue-jet-gapgen =
    .role = Airborne gap generator
    .lore = An unarmed radar plane that hides the ground below it from the enemy. Order it over an area and it circles there. Cover a tank push with it.
catalogue-lsat =
    .role = Orbital weapon
    .lore = Hovers high above the map and fires a laser straight down at enemies below it. Satellites within 12 cells link into a mesh that strengthens the beam. Only ASAT sites can reach it.
catalogue-jet-f104 =
    .role = Interceptor, tier 2
    .lore = The Starflash: a needle-nosed Cold War interceptor built for raw speed. Its missiles hit buildings and vehicles hard, but it has little armour.
catalogue-jet-f4 =
    .role = Interceptor, tier 2
    .lore = The Spectre II: a rugged twin-engine workhorse flown by more nations than any other jet in the game. Reliable strike power at a fair price.
catalogue-jet-f14 =
    .role = Interceptor, tier 3
    .lore = The Bobcat: a swing-wing fleet defender with long-range missiles. Flown only by the USA and Iran.
catalogue-jet-f16 =
    .role = Multirole fighter, tier 3
    .lore = The Fighting Kestrel: a light, agile multirole fighter. Good value for strikes on vehicles and buildings.
catalogue-jet-a10 =
    .role = Ground attack, tier 3
    .lore = The Thunderhog: a flying tank built around a huge rotary cannon. Heavily armoured, slow and lethal to armour. Keep fighters away from it.
catalogue-jet-f117 =
    .role = Stealth strike, tier 3
    .lore = The Nightjar: a faceted stealth jet that slips past air defences to hit high-value targets.
catalogue-jet-sr71 =
    .role = Reconnaissance, tier 3
    .lore = The Blackwing: a high-speed reconnaissance jet that is very hard to catch. It reveals the enemy base on its way through.
catalogue-jet-b52 =
    .role = Heavy bomber, tier 2
    .lore = The Stratoforce: a huge carpet-bomber that levels whole blocks of a base. Escort it, because it can't defend itself against fighters.
catalogue-jet-f22 =
    .role = Stealth fighter, tier 5
    .lore = The Raptorex: a fifth-generation stealth fighter and the best Union air superiority jet. Fast, hard to see and deadly.
catalogue-jet-b2 =
    .role = Stealth bomber, tier 5
    .lore = The Wraith: a flying-wing stealth bomber that delivers a massive bomb load deep behind enemy lines.
catalogue-jet-yf23 =
    .role = Prototype fighter
    .lore = The Black Recluse: an experimental stealth fighter. Only one per player, a rare and lethal ace.
catalogue-bmbf =
    .role = Superweapon airfield
    .lore = A guarded bomber field with one giant pad, a hangar and an armoured bomb bunker. It houses the AB-35 Longwing and charges the Fatman Strike while the bomber lives. USA only, one per player.
catalogue-yb35 =
    .role = Atomic bomber
    .lore = The Longwing: a flying-wing bomber with four pusher propellers. It carries no guns. When the Fatman Strike is ready it takes off, drops the Fatman atomic bomb on the target and flies home. Lose it and the strike timer starts over. USA only, one per player.
catalogue-weapon-fatman = Fatman atomic bomb
catalogue-sbmb =
    .role = Superweapon airfield
    .lore = A Soviet-style bomber base with one huge pad, an arched hangar and a thermonuclear weapons vault. It houses the Tv-95 Bear and charges the Thermonuclear Strike while the bomber lives. Russia only, one per player.
catalogue-tu95 =
    .role = Thermonuclear bomber
    .lore = The Bear: a long-range bomber with four contra-rotating propeller engines. Unarmed, it flies one mission: when the Thermonuclear Strike is ready it drops the RDS-37 hydrogen bomb and flies home. Lose it and the strike timer starts over. Russia only, one per player.
catalogue-weapon-rds37 = RDS-37 hydrogen bomb
catalogue-zolf =
    .role = Ballistic missile truck
    .lore = A heavy wheeled launcher with two short-range ballistic missiles on its erector. It outranges every other ground unit; only long-range air defence can stop the missiles. Iran only.
catalogue-weapon-zolf_srbm = Zolfaghar ballistic missiles
catalogue-m16 =
    .role = Anti-air vehicle
    .lore = A halftrack with four heavy machine guns on a turning mount. Cheap and quick: it shreds helicopters, low jets and infantry, but tanks shrug it off.
catalogue-weapon-quadfifty = Quad .50 machine guns
catalogue-flak =
    .role = Anti-air defence
    .lore = A heavy twin flak gun on a turning mount. Its bursts hurt every aircraft nearby, and it can knock drones and cruise missiles out of the sky.
catalogue-weapon-flakcannon = Twin flak guns
catalogue-cg =
    .role = Missile cruiser
    .lore = A guided-missile cruiser: Tomahawks reach targets far inland, while its SAMs and close-in gun cover the fleet from the air. USA only.
catalogue-weapon-tomahawkship = Tomahawk cruise missiles
catalogue-bb =
    .role = Battleship
    .lore = The biggest guns at sea: three-gun 16-inch turrets fore and aft that shell the coast from beyond the reach of most defences. Slow and very hard to sink, but blind to submarines.
catalogue-weapon-16inch = 16-inch naval guns
catalogue-hcru =
    .role = Helicopter cruiser
    .lore = A cruiser with a helicopter deck aft: missiles and a gatling gun against aircraft, depth charges and sonar against submarines.
catalogue-lha =
    .role = Amphibious assault ship
    .lore = A flat-deck assault ship that carries a whole landing group to the beach and fights off aircraft on the way. USA only.
catalogue-btr =
    .role = Armoured transport
    .lore = An eight-wheeled armoured personnel carrier with a turret autocannon: quick on roads, it drops 5 infantry at the front and keeps shooting. Russia only.
catalogue-mi35 =
    .role = Assault helicopter
    .lore = The flying tank: an armoured gunship with a chain gun and rocket pods, and a cabin for 5 soldiers. It strafes the landing zone, then drops its squad into it.
catalogue-ka52 =
    .role = Attack helicopter
    .lore = The Alligator: two coaxial rotors and no tail rotor make it fast and agile. Anti-tank missiles and a 30 mm cannon hunt armour. Russia only.
catalogue-kvst =
    .role = Assault walker
    .lore = A heavy tank hull with a 152 mm gun, carried on two armoured legs instead of tracks. Slow, but it strides over walls, trenches and anyone in its way.
catalogue-weapon-kv152 = 152 mm walker gun
catalogue-mtrk =
    .role = Crusher
    .lore = A civilian off-roader on giant wheels, pressed into service. It carries no weapon at all: it simply drives over infantry, fences and sandbag walls. USA only.
catalogue-hmmv =
    .role = Scout car
    .lore = The workhorse of the US Army: armoured, quick, with a .50 cal on the roof and room for a fire team of four. USA only.
catalogue-weapon-hmmv_m2 = .50 cal machine gun
catalogue-sfng =
    .role = Experimental tank
    .lore = A cyber tank from the Project X labs. Its main gun throws a heavy electric discharge that cooks armour from the inside. Only one can be fielded.
catalogue-weapon-shockfangzap = Shock cannon
catalogue-wbot =
    .role = Combat mech
    .lore = A two-legged war machine with a rotary chain gun on one arm and an anti-tank rocket pod on the other. It walks where tanks cannot.
catalogue-mi17 =
    .role = Troop helicopter
    .lore = The Hip: the Vanguard's workhorse helicopter. It lifts a full squad of eight to the front, with a door gun to keep heads down at the landing zone.
catalogue-aw101 =
    .role = Heavy transport helicopter
    .lore = The Merlin: a fast three-engined helicopter that carries ten soldiers over long distances. India only.
catalogue-weapon-jetagm-ataka = 9M120 Ataka anti-tank missiles
catalogue-weapon-jetagm-hot = HOT anti-tank missiles
catalogue-weapon-jetrockets = Hydra rocket pods
catalogue-weapon-jetrockets-s8 = S-8 rocket pods
catalogue-weapon-jetrockets-s8-ripple = S-8 rocket pods (ripple fire)
catalogue-weapon-jetrockets-ripple = Rocket pods (ripple fire)
catalogue-weapon-jetgun-gsh30 = 30 mm cannon
catalogue-weapon-jetgun-m61 = 20 mm cannon
catalogue-mlrs =
    .role = Rocket tank
    .lore = A tracked multiple rocket launcher. It empties its entire rack in a few seconds, a heavy stream of 19 rockets that blankets the target area, then needs a long time to reload.
catalogue-weapon-mlrs_stream = 19-rocket salvo
catalogue-hlfr =
    .role = Rocket truck
    .lore = A wheeled multiple rocket launcher with a bank of closed launch tubes. It ripples off 30 light rockets in a long stream that saturates the target area, then reloads.
catalogue-weapon-hlfr_stream = 30-rocket stream
catalogue-tiger =
    .role = Heavy attack helicopter
    .lore = The Tiger: a Franco-German gunship with HOT anti-tank missiles on its outer racks and rocket pods that ripple off a stream of 68 mm rockets. France and Germany only.
catalogue-jet-x47 =
    .role = Combat drone prototype
    .lore = The Stingray: an unmanned combat drone. Cheap and fragile, but it strafes infantry and light armour without risking a pilot. One per player.
catalogue-jet-v22 =
    .role = Tiltrotor transport, tier 4
    .lore = The Kestrel tiltrotor takes off like a helicopter and flies like a plane, carrying infantry far behind enemy lines. Unarmed.
catalogue-jet-harrier =
    .role = VTOL jump jet, tier 3
    .lore = The Harrow takes off vertically from tiny pads and carrier decks and hits vehicles hard.
catalogue-jet-m2000 =
    .role = Multirole fighter, tier 3
    .lore = The Mirago 2000: a sleek delta-wing multirole fighter used by many nations.
catalogue-jet-rafale =
    .role = Multirole fighter, tier 4
    .lore = The Rafal F4: a modern canard-delta omnirole fighter, as good at strikes as at dogfights.
catalogue-jet-typhoon =
    .role = Multirole fighter, tier 4
    .lore = The Typhon: a European canard-delta fighter with great agility and a heavy strike load.
catalogue-jet-vulcan =
    .role = Heavy bomber, tier 2
    .lore = The Volcan: a delta-wing V-bomber, England's long-range heavy hitter against bases.
catalogue-jet-seavixen =
    .role = Naval strike, tier 2
    .lore = The Sea Vixa: a twin-boom naval strike fighter that specialises in sinking ships.
catalogue-jet-mig3 =
    .role = Piston fighter, tier 0
    .lore = The MiK-3 Strela: a 1940s propeller fighter. Cheap and quick to build, good for strafing infantry and light vehicles.
catalogue-jet-la11 =
    .role = Piston fighter, tier 0
    .lore = The LaV-11 Fang: a rugged radial-engine fighter from the 1940s. Cheap and fast to field in numbers.
catalogue-jet-mig21 =
    .role = Jet fighter, tier 2
    .lore = The MiK-21 Fishbone: the most widely flown jet in the Vanguard bloc. Simple, fast and cheap.
catalogue-jet-mig23 =
    .role = Multirole fighter, tier 3
    .lore = The MiK-23 Flintlock: a swing-wing fighter-bomber that strikes fast and leaves fast.
catalogue-jet-mig25 =
    .role = Interceptor, tier 3
    .lore = The MiK-25 Foxbane: a brutally fast high-altitude interceptor. Few things can catch it.
catalogue-jet-su25 =
    .role = Ground attack, tier 3
    .lore = The Sk-25 Rook: an armoured close-support jet that hammers tanks and vehicles at low level.
catalogue-jet-su27 =
    .role = Air superiority, tier 3
    .lore = The Sk-27 Flankard: a large twin-engine fighter with long range and a heavy weapons load.
catalogue-jet-su35 =
    .role = Multirole fighter, tier 4
    .lore = The Sk-35 Flankard-E: thrust-vectoring supermanoeuvrability and the Vanguard's best mainstream fighter.
catalogue-jet-tu160 =
    .role = Strategic bomber, tier 3
    .lore = The Tv-160 Swanwing: Russia's supersonic swing-wing bomber, which delivers a massive payload at high speed.
catalogue-jet-su47 =
    .role = Prototype fighter
    .lore = The Sk-47 Berkov: an experimental forward-swept-wing stealth fighter. One per player.
catalogue-jet-yak141 =
    .role = VTOL prototype
    .lore = The Yk-141 Freestyler: a supersonic VTOL jump jet prototype that strikes vehicles. One per player.
catalogue-jet-grom =
    .role = Combat drone prototype
    .lore = The Grom-K: a Russian unmanned combat drone. Cheap, fragile and dangerous to infantry. One per player.
catalogue-jet-zeppelin =
    .role = Bombing airship
    .lore = An armoured airship with an enormous bomb load. Very slow, but a fully loaded Zeppelin over a base is devastating. Shoot it down early.
catalogue-jet-l39 =
    .role = Light attack, tier 2
    .lore = The L-39U Albatross: a light attack trainer that is surprisingly effective against infantry, light armour and drones.
catalogue-jet-an225 =
    .role = Heavy transport, tier 4
    .lore = The An-225 Dreamer: the largest aircraft ever built. It carries infantry across the map. Unarmed.
catalogue-jet-j20 =
    .role = Stealth fighter, tier 5
    .lore = The JX-20 Jade Dragon: China's fifth-generation stealth fighter, long-ranged and hard to see.
catalogue-jet-swarm =
    .role = Drone swarm, tier 3
    .lore = Turkey's Swarm Drones: cheap unmanned attackers that overwhelm infantry and light armour in numbers.
catalogue-jet-saeqeh =
    .role = Jet fighter, tier 3
    .lore = The Saeqa: Iran's twin-tailed home-built fighter, a solid strike jet against vehicles and buildings.
catalogue-jet-qaher =
    .role = Stealth prototype
    .lore = The Qahir-X: Iran's experimental stealth fighter. One per player.

## Naval
catalogue-pt =
    .role = Gunboat
    .lore = A light, fast patrol boat that detects submarines and hunts small ships. Cheap eyes on the water.
catalogue-dd =
    .role = Destroyer
    .lore = A fast multi-role warship that detects submarines and fights ships, vehicles and aircraft. The backbone of a Union fleet.
catalogue-ca =
    .role = Cruiser
    .lore = A very slow ship with huge long-range guns that shell coastal bases from far out at sea. Escort it with destroyers against submarines.
catalogue-lst =
    .role = Landing craft
    .lore = Carries infantry and tanks across water and lands them on any beach. Unarmed.
catalogue-ss =
    .role = Attack submarine
    .lore = Submerges out of sight and torpedoes ships. It detects other submarines. Only surfaces to fire.
catalogue-msub =
    .role = Missile submarine
    .lore = A submerged siege platform that fires missiles at buildings, ground units and aircraft deep inland. Weak against other ships.
catalogue-cv1 =
    .role = Fleet carrier
    .lore = An Essex-class carrier from the Second World War: a floating airbase with SAM launchers for defence. Launches and rearms jets at sea.
catalogue-cv2 =
    .role = Battle carrier
    .lore = The first nuclear-powered carrier, Enterprise class: a bigger deck, tougher hull and more SAM launchers.
catalogue-cv3 =
    .role = Supercarrier
    .lore = A Nimitz-class nuclear supercarrier, the heavily armoured flagship of the fleet.
catalogue-cv4 =
    .role = Next-gen supercarrier
    .lore = A Gerald R. Ford-class carrier with the latest defences. The most powerful ship afloat.
catalogue-cvgb =
    .role = Carrier (England)
    .lore = The Royal Navy's Queen Elizabeth carrier, with a ski-jump bow and twin islands.
catalogue-cvfr =
    .role = Carrier (France)
    .lore = The Charles de Gaulle, France's nuclear-powered carrier and the pride of the Marine nationale.
catalogue-cvjp =
    .role = Light carrier (Japan)
    .lore = The Kaga: a helicopter destroyer rebuilt as a light carrier for jump-jet fighters.
catalogue-cvit =
    .role = Light carrier (Italy)
    .lore = The Cavour: an Italian light carrier for jump jets and helicopters.
catalogue-cveg =
    .role = Helicopter carrier (Egypt)
    .lore = The Mistral: an amphibious helicopter carrier. Cheap and quick to build.
catalogue-cvsu =
    .role = Aviation cruiser
    .lore = The Kiev: half carrier, half cruiser, with a flight deck aft and missile launchers forward.
catalogue-cvru =
    .role = Carrier (Russia)
    .lore = The Kuznetsov: a heavy aircraft-carrying cruiser with a ski-jump bow and strong SAM defences.
catalogue-cvin =
    .role = Carrier (India)
    .lore = The Vikrant: India's home-built carrier with a ski-jump bow.
catalogue-cvcn =
    .role = Supercarrier (China)
    .lore = The Fujian: China's newest supercarrier, with electromagnetic catapults.
catalogue-cvtr =
    .role = Drone carrier (Turkey)
    .lore = The Anadolu: an amphibious ship turned drone carrier that launches swarms of attack drones.
catalogue-cvir =
    .role = Drone carrier (Iran)
    .lore = The Bagheri: a converted merchant ship with a flight deck for drones. Cheap, but fragile.
